ivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"}}}